<<~ ahu slot=`#/purpose`>>

`outcome-reads.ts` reads the answer ring and a write's verdict row, and waits for an outcome to land on either. The ring answers first and the row second, so a body answers while the ring holds it and its verdict after it left. A wait's timer paces this side alone and never decides the act. The DAM checklist (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/uds-channel-dam`>>) carries its observations.

<<~/ahu>>

